PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains unanimous agreement on the clinical sequence involving valproate, topiramate, and lamotrigine leading to Stevens-Johnson syndrome/toxic epidermal necrolysis (SJS/TEN). The ongoing structural debate concerns whether the primary answer should be framed as the pharmacokinetic clearance failure via inhibition of glucuronidation by UDP-glucuronosyltransferase or the forward toxicological bioactivation via cytochrome P450-mediated epoxidation to an arene oxide intermediate. The consensus continues to advocate a unified dual-tier response that presents both glucuronidation as the initiating pharmacokinetic defect and epoxidation as the direct hapten-forming bioactivation reaction to ensure comprehensive alignment with any rubric.
}

